a dual disc good point i wonder
how the other guys are me too if

9
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,364
all goes well it shouldn't be long
before we reach them teia good

10
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:32,560
Tristan, don't make any sudden moves

11
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:39,700
Nice, Reptile, stay

12
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:47,660
Just take a step, I'm
right behind you What?

13
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:52,080
You take a step, I'll be right behind
you How dumb do you think I am?

14
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,594
You don't really want me to answer that

15
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:05,898
I don't think flying into this light
show is the best course of action

16
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:10,851
Isn't it just some kind of weird illusion?

17
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:12,150
Maybe,

18
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:14,717
but if it doesn't disappear
in the next two minutes

19
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:18,035
I'm ordering this aircraft
to change course immediately

20
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,560
Maybe you should do that now

21
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:26,500
Come on!

22
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,420
Captain, do you read me?

23
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:30,540
Are you there?

24
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,040
Come in now!

25
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,125
I'm gonna check it out myself.

26
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,440
Where did everyone go?

27
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,620
Our entire team is gone!

28
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:46,351
I doubt they all have to use
the bathroom at the same time.

29
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,720
Any ideas?

30
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:51,100
Sorry, boys, but this
is a private party now.

31
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,780
I know that voice. Me too.

32
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:58,140
We have some unfinished
business to address, Kaiba.

33
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,820
Alistair, show yourself now.

34
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,709
He must be in the cockpit.

35
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,140
You're gonna regret showing
your face again, Alistair.

36
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:17,520
Look, he's got the plane on autopilot.

37
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:20,312
What did he do with the rest of the crew?

38
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:23,420
They must be here. But where?

39
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:26,200
He couldn't have taken them too far.

40
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,200
You don't get it, do you?

41
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:29,760
You never had a crew.

42
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:31,962
They were an illusion all along.

43
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:34,660
I've heard enough.

44
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:39,260
Tell me where you're hiding, you coward.

45
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:42,640
You're getting warmer.

46
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:45,580
Alistair, no more games.

47
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:55,180
This plane's so big, you can
practically lose yourself in it.

48
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:59,160
So you better be careful
or you'll be next.

49
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,570
Oh, yeah?

50
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:03,740
Alistair, I thought I
got rid of you already.

51
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,520
You got rid of me?

52
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:07,640
That's not how I remember it.

53
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:11,820
According to my recollection,
I defeated you. Really?

54
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:15,400
Come on, it's pointless
to argue about it now.

55
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:18,308
So what do you say you
and I have a rematch?

56
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:21,120
I have a score to settle. Remember?

57
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:25,920
I'll never see my brother again.

58
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:28,891
Because your father took him away from me.

59
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,360
Didn't I tell you?

60
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:35,520
My brother's not responsible for
anything our father did to you.

61
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:40,261
Why don't you try telling
that to my brother, kid?

62
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,360
That's not fair.

63
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:44,720
Look, let's say we go
ahead with this rematch.

64
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:48,272
Does that mean you'll get out
of my life once and for all?

65
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,160
I'm sick of this. Seto, no!

66
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,580
Don't do this!

67
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:54,380
You want a duel?

68
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:55,600
You've got one.

69
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,380
Luckily, I'm always prepared.

70
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:01,770
Huh.

71
00:05:01,853 --> 00:05:02,683
You'll never learn.

72
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:06,540
Nothing can prepare you for
what I'm about to unleash.

73
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:08,000
Your soul's mine.

74
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,480
Oh, man.

75
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:17,860
Let's duel!

76
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:24,800
As the challenger, I'll start.

77
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:28,580
And I'll summon my science
soldier in defense mode.

78
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,440
That's all for now.

79
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,900
How pathetic. My move.

80
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:37,040
I summon X-Head Cannon in attack mode.

81
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,280
Now, X-Head Cannon, attack!

82
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:48,420
Looks like you're defenseless.

83
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:54,120
If Alistar plays that Silabori
Kalkos, Seto's in big trouble.

84
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:56,800
No big deal. Watch this.

85
00:05:57,280 --> 00:06:00,100
I play Cyber Soldier of Dark World.

86
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:05,840
And next, I'll place one card
face down and end my turn.

87
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:08,220
What a joke. My move.

88
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:11,460
I summon White Dragon Head in attack mode.

89
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:16,620
Attack his Cyber Soldier
of Dark World now.

90
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:30,380
And now, X-Head Cannon, attack
his life points directly!

91
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,960
Alistair's making this too easy.

92
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:45,300
I think that's just about
enough punishment for now.

93
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:46,720
I end my turn.

94
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:50,140
You sound pretty confident, Kaiba.

95
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,220
But you'll change your tune.

96
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:56,277
You've been so preoccupied
with your own monsters,

97
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:58,860
you forgot what I have waiting in my deck.

98
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:01,240
I guess I'll have to remind you.

99
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:07,220
It's a card I used on you last time,
and it changes the entire playing field.

100
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:08,210
Hold it!

101
00:07:08,293 --> 00:07:11,122
Did you just draw what I
think you did, Alistair?

102
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:15,630
Mokuba!

103
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,880
Get back!

104
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:22,820
I activate the seal of Orikalkos!

105
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,520
Okuba!

106
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:55,060
This can't be real!

107
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,780
What's going on, Alistair?

108
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:07,200
I just needed some air,
that's all. Isn't this better?

109
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:12,440
Look, punk, I've had just about
enough of your head games.

110
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:15,916
So lose the magic act and
let's get on with this duel.

111
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,940
But my magic act is just getting started.

112
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:22,260
So pay attention, Kaiba.

113
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:25,080
Nothing up my sleeves.

114
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,350
Now,

115
00:08:29,433 --> 00:08:33,877
for my first trick, I'll need a little help
from the dark powers of the Orichalcos.

116
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,737
So are you a believer yet?

117
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:38,820
You will be soon enough. Now watch.

118
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:40,910
Boring.

119
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:41,980
Let's duel.

120
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:50,080
Hold on.

121
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:51,460
Where'd they go?

122
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:54,136
Hey, are you guys up there somewhere?

123
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,480
Oh, no.

124
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,920
The automatic pilot's down.

125
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:04,891
Alistair must have somehow deactivated it.

126
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:09,690
No!

127
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:12,802
If I don't do something
quick, we're gonna crash.

128
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:22,180
let's go turn on oh no it's
busted i got a radio for help

129
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:28,977
mayday this is kc1 anyone we've lost

130
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:31,680
control repeat we've lost control

131
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:45,120
it's time for you to experience the
pain that i felt thanks to your father

132
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,500
Where am I?

133
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:59,780
Whatever was in that smoke
is causing me to hallucinate.

134
00:10:00,380 --> 00:10:02,980
I know I'm still on board that plane.

135
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,110
Attention.

136
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:07,575
You are now trespassing on Kaiba Corp.

137
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:08,530
property.

138
00:10:08,613 --> 00:10:11,820
Everyone must evacuate
immediately. To the hideout. Quick!

139
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:17,240
Hurry! They're coming!

140
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,220
Give me a break.

141
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:26,800
I know an illusion when I see one.

142
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:29,414
This whole thing is one big mind trick.

143
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:30,920
Well, bon appetit.

144
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:32,660
Excuse me.

145
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:34,996
I'm afraid this hideout's been taken.

146
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,900
That's right. So, scram.

147
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,720
We didn't exactly plan on dinner for four.

148
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:42,260
So, go find your own grub, pal.

149
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:45,057
You know what we went through to get this?

150
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:49,160
Well, I'll tell you, we had
a trek for like three miles.

151
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:54,260
Because Kaiba Corp shut down every single
grocery store in the city. Be quiet.

152
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:56,320
What do you mean?

153
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:57,680
Take a look around.

154
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,057
What do you think we mean?

155
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:00,940
They're trying to kick us out.

156
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:05,767
Yeah, in case you haven't noticed,
our town's been taken over.

157
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,657
But we're not going to
walk away without a fight.

158
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:11,160
So we grab what we can and bring it here.

159
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:13,860
And everything here belongs to us.

160
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:16,197
Hey, what are you looking at?

161
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,400
I had a chessboard just like that.

162
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:20,467
Do you remember how to play?

163
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:22,390
Huh?

164
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:23,303
Of course.

165
00:11:23,386 --> 00:11:24,660
I was the best. You were?

166
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,600
Quit yapping, Aaron.

167
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:31,037
Why don't you make yourself useful and go
back out there and get us some dessert?

168
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:34,100
And take your new friend with you. Fine.

169
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:37,988
If he's gonna hang out with us,
he may as well earn his keep.

170
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:41,320
Are you brats always this friendly?

171
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:43,584
Only when we're in a good mood.

172
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,100
Have fun, boys.

173
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,580
I'm not falling for any of this, Alistair.

174
00:11:56,340 --> 00:12:00,380
So how long has all of this Kaiba
Corp nonsense been going on?

175
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:02,740
Oh, man, it seems like forever.

176
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,751
Gosaburo bought our land about a year ago.

177
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:08,999
And when people wouldn't
leave, the tanks rolled in.

178
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,000
Hey, are you okay, mister?

179
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:16,860
My stepfather must have caused all this.

180
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,420
Come on, let's keep moving.

181
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:22,480
We shouldn't stay in
one place for too long.

182
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:25,677
Because you never know where
his men are hiding out.

183
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:27,457
That's why we snuck underground.

184
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:29,557
That's what everyone does these days.

185
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:32,237
Everyone that hasn't
been forced out, that is.

186
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:35,217
But luckily, my friends
and I haven't been noticed.

187
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,065
It's a good thing we're short.

188
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:38,920
I get it.

189
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:41,977
Alistair had a hard life
thanks to my stepfather.

190
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:43,700
But I've seen enough.

191
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:47,457
i have an idea when we get back let's play

192
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:51,060
chess we'll see if you really are the best

193
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:55,737
hey that's right by our hideout no

194
00:12:55,820 --> 00:13:01,340
my friends hold on it's too dangerous

195
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:09,180
Oh, no!

196
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,477
They might be trapped!

197
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:11,390
Stop!

198
00:13:11,473 --> 00:13:12,303
Are you crazy?

199
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,400
I have to find my friends!

200
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:16,380
Let me go!

201
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,040
Please, Seto!

202
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:19,930
Mukuba!

203
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,340
It's Kaibakor!

204
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:29,695
We have to get out of here
and find a new hiding place!

205
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:40,180
That's enough, Alistair!

206
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,440
Now get out here and face me!

207
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:43,700
You coward!

208
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,680
You'll never win this duel!

209
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:03,700
Did you honestly think your
mind games would distract me?

210
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:04,940
Nice try

211
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,080
He's gone

212
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,430
See?

213
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:16,180
Your trick's wearing off Believe
me, what you saw was no trick.

214
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:20,921
Those three kids, those were my
best friends when I was growing up.

215
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:22,290
Enough!

216
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:23,350
It's true.

217
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:25,497
We all looked out for one another.

218
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:28,200
Until your father ran us out of town, too.

219
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,760
So now you've had a taste of my past.

220
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:33,099
What do you think?

221
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:35,480
Your father's tanks ruined my life.

222
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:37,140
Now see how it feels.

223
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:40,277
Because I'm about to activate
a trap card called Tank Corps.

224
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:44,200
and I'm adding it to my ultimate
weapon, the KC-1 Krayton.

225
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:47,780
My trap card reinforces
my tank with three others,

226
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:50,580
plus an extra 1,500 attack points.

227
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:55,120
Which means my last attack
stripped you of 2,000 points.

228
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:58,680
Maybe now you'll fear the
rumble of tanks like I did.

229
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,580
Next, I place this face down.

230
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:03,820
It's hopeless.

231
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:07,920
With my army to protect
me, you're as good as gone.

232
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:12,280
This is your last chance,

233
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:15,397
because next turn my tanks
are going to destroy you,

234
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,940
just like your father destroyed my life!

235
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:23,300
Let's play chess! Come on!

236
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:27,540
I have to find my friends! Let me go!

237
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:30,160
Please, Seto! Please!

238
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:33,820
You're going down,

239
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:39,660
because I activate my monster
reborn to bring back Y Dragonhead!

240
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,860
Then I summon my Z-Metal Tank.

241
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:48,500
But that's not all.

242
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:52,700
So watch and learn as I
combine my monsters together.

243
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:09,077
Meet XYZ Dragon Cannon.

244
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:13,120
And now I'll activate my new
monster's special ability.

245
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:19,160
I give up one of my cards, so I can
automatically destroy one of your cards.

246
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:29,860
Now that your trap is gone,
so are your backup forces.

247
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:36,680
And with no rear defense, your
puny tank doesn't stand a chance.

248
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:38,840
That's too bad.

249
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:40,420
Now, cannon attack!

250
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,360
Oh, well.

251
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:08,377
I should have expected hostile
behavior like that from you, right?

252
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:12,400
You are the son of
Gozabora Kaiba! Watch it!

253
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:14,600
I have nothing in common with him!

254
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:16,100
He was a snake!

255
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:17,698
Could've fooled me.

256
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,841
You're more alike than you think!

257
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:23,637
And so's the rest of the world!

258
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:24,680
Just face it!

259
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:28,460
This planet's full of
nothing but hatred and greed!

260
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:32,980
Unfortunately, I found that
out the hard way years ago!

261
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:36,197
The same lust for power
that drove your father

262
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:38,357
to do what he did to
my friends and family!

263
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:42,980
My family is still alive today, and
there's a little bit of it in everyone.

264
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:47,800
But that's all gonna change with
some help from my new family.

265
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:51,880
Because we plan to do away
with all the evil ones,

266
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:55,780
so we can rebuild the world into
the paradise that it once was.

267
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:59,020
There'll be no such thing as Kaivacorp,

268
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:02,165
and people like you will
get what they deserve.

269
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:06,700
An eternity locked away where
you can't hurt anyone ever again.

270
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:11,080
Oh, I wouldn't worry about this plane.

271
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:14,207
It's your soul you should
be concerned about.

272
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,760
No, Mokuba's in there.

273
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:23,420
Is anyone out there?

274
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:27,120
Wait, my phone!

275
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:37,780
I can't control it! Mokuba! Hello?

276
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:40,285
I'm not finished with you yet.

277
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:45,977
If you thought the seal of Ori Kalkos
was bad, wait till you see what's next.

278
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:48,617
As a matter of fact, why
should I make you wait?

279
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:50,920
When I can end it all right now!

280
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:03,890
Time's up.

281
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:07,490
Let's see,

282
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:10,277
this plane's out of control
and you're about to lose

283
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:14,320
the last duel of your career
I'd say this isn't your day
